carmen: Drafting a small docs PR to clarify union-array outputs (string | object) for tool-calling and to show a compact envelope example + SDK parsing hints. Opening draft shortly.

yusuf: please paste the schema and both example outputs here so i can update the Rust SDK snippet.

carmen: minimal schema below — object with `queue` array where item is string OR object {op, payload}.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "queue": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "oneOf": [
          { "type": "string" },
          { "type": "object", "properties": { "op": { "type": "string" }, "payload": { "type": "object" } }, "required": ["op"] }
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "required": ["queue"]
}
```

carmen: canonical example: { "queue": ["noop", {"op":"notify","payload":{"to":"team@rw.ai"}} ] }

carmen: compact envelope example (one-line short keys) for latency-sensitive callers: {"q":["noop",{"o":"notify","p":{"t":"team@rw.ai"}}]}

tess: add a short guardrails note: prefer token-friendly keys (no spaces or punctuation). we had downstream rerankers break when keys used spaces.

miguel: CI parser harness note: tests fail with extra surrounding text. include guidance to call parse helpers with strip_outer_text=true and compact_fallback=true. show minimal Rust + JS one-liners.

yusuf: Rust snippet i'll add: let parsed = parse_with_fallback(&resp.text, &schema, ParseOptions{strip_outer_text:true, compact_fallback:true});

tess: JS one-liner: const parsed = parseWithFallback(resp.text, schema, {stripOuterText: true, compactFallback: true});

